Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Topological Properties", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell["\<\
The topological properties of a substrate are read off its metric balls. The \
closed balls of one radius r generate a topology: a vertex q lies in the \
closure of a vertex p when the r-ball at p is contained in the r-ball at q. \
BallTopology returns this specialization preorder as a digraph, and closure, \
interior, boundary, neighbourhood and continuity are computed on it. A family \
of balls forms a complex through its intersections: a simplex is admitted \
when every k of its balls have a common point, so k = 2 gives the \
Vietoris-Rips complex of twice the radius, k = Infinity the Cech complex, and \
the orders between interpolate. The least number N(r) of balls of radius r \
that cover the substrate falls as r grows, and the rate of that fall is a \
dimension. The intersection of all closed balls containing a set of points is \
its ball hull, the smallest ball-convex set containing it. Three things still \
wait: the covering dimension as a function, the intersection of the balls of \
one radius r containing a set, and, as a tutorial rather than a function, the \
dimension read from where the intersection of the balls containing k given \
points becomes degenerate.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection",
 CellID->1866139230,ExpressionUUID->"a0ea3657-4c83-4862-93c8-ecf80cebc774"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The ball topology", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"d646b1d2-c455-42b6-a3fb-83903c8bf72d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallTopology",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the Hasse diagram of the r-ball specialization preorder: an \
edge q -> p when the closed r-ball at p lies inside the one at q"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a2ad208a-7aa8-44df-9a6f-319376b74227"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TopologicalClosure",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the closure of a vertex list in the preorder digraph, the \
union of the down-sets of its vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f3f0ee6f-b8f3-42f1-9971-57720b592503"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TopologicalInterior",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the interior of a vertex list in the preorder digraph, the \
complement of the closure of its complement"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"5b83a03a-8450-4b80-b156-47c165263a9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TopologicalBoundary",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the two-sided boundary of a vertex list, its closure minus its \
interior"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"47f5e96c-2da2-436c-b1aa-4d8edd3c86cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TopologicalNeighborhood",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the smallest open set containing a vertex list, the union of \
the up-sets of its vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0696c672-e7b1-458e-ae9a-b8417dc7ea4a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ContinuousMapQ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] whether a vertex map is continuous from one preorder digraph \
to another"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"af0e0079-144a-4a10-af88-3c25b287cd0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TopologyGraph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the graph drawn with the Hasse arrows of a preorder digraph on \
top"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"8b2d4ca6-9b8d-40d6-8ed9-9109c53d3f29"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The ball intersection complex", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"3d206014-e1a8-4b45-acf9-e72332cb196b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallIntersectionComplex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the order-k complex of closed radius-r balls: a simplex is \
admitted when every k of its balls have a common point"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0e088993-878e-48d3-ad58-c554863972af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CechComplex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the nerve of the closed radius-r balls, the order-Infinity \
ball intersection complex"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"1ee0a81c-f9d6-43f6-974e-cf92a0f07e83"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MiniballRadius",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the radius of the smallest ball enclosing a set of points"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"855ee424-6e1a-415a-937f-7933dfd8ced0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallIntersectionFiltrationValue",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the birth radius of a simplex in the order-k complex"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"6014ea9f-6015-466f-a216-462f68b6234f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallIntersectionFiltration",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the order-k complexes over a list of radii, ready for \
persistence"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"7b77619c-1e1f-4e0f-b960-320996d5bc55"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CechFiltration",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the Cech complexes over a list of radii"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"b9c7b59d-72b8-450b-a527-ef86ba9d2f89"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallIntersectionBifiltration",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the complexes over the radius and the order together"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"7621b560-962f-4e55-8ae8-f739f54d6cad"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Ball covers and the covering dimension", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"463f517e-5ea8-4e5c-b81f-d1419e258e09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["FindBallCover",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] a smallest set of centres whose radius-r balls cover every \
vertex, or a given set of targets"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"2cef02d0-960e-4df9-a381-1337b391948f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallCoverQ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] whether the radius-r balls about a set of centres cover every \
vertex, or a given set of targets"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9a53581d-16b5-4eed-89a6-f043b03e19d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["DominationNumber",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the size N(r) of a smallest radius-r ball cover"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d1ec5caf-162b-454d-ad5e-d88ca0309b18"],

Cell["\<\
waits: the covering dimension, from how N(r) falls as r grows, or from how \
many balls of radius r cover a ball of radius 2r\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"27f9c866-9e99-49e3-bbca-12ee041054cd"],

Cell["\<\
waits, as a tutorial: the dimension read from where the intersection of the \
balls containing k given points becomes degenerate\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"00156fbe-b61f-47eb-8d71-bea6b3438fe6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Ball hulls", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"428294cd-9b05-474b-ad31-5bd82aa1c8ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BallHull",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the intersection of all closed balls containing a vertex set, \
the smallest ball-convex superset"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"874e84ee-eb1c-451f-af8e-bc0ac914fa9b"],

